34,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Oh no! I found out that some roads close in winter and the bus links in the outer wards are gone! People have to travel an hour now!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings are equally telling. A digitisation project from years ago failed to index half its images, while partner-run groups are still thriving unaided.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"We have a skill gap. We have retired tradespeople volunteering, but no one on the payroll is trained to supervise outside facilitators.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The funding is precarious. Grants only cover session fees for a year, and last year's vehicle running costs overran by a third.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I saw that the outer wards had huge attendance at outreach stops—more than the main building gets midweek. They really need us.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Minako, if the vehicle costs are so high, maybe a mobile service is too expensive? But @Daisuke's data shows that's where the people are!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the issue isn't just cost, but reliability. If the roads close and the buses are gone, a fixed schedule is a fragile promise.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, the ""partner-run"" success you mentioned is interesting. It suggests that if we don't rely on internal payroll for supervision, we might succeed.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, that is a point, but we must remember that after the first year, the operating budget must absorb the costs. We cannot rely on temporary grants.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm worried... if we just put something in the main branch, the people in the outer wards will just keep being left behind.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Yumi,,But we have to do something! Maybe something that doesn't depend on the roads? Or something that uses those great volunteers Shion found?,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"We must avoid the ""digitisation trap""—starting something ambitious that becomes a mess of unindexed data because we lacked the long-term discipline.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Exactly. Any proposal requiring certified technicians or internal supervisors is a risk, as our current roster is lacking in those specific areas.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We also need to consider that equipment allocations were handed back to reserves. We have capital, but our operational spending is volatile.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"If we can't go to them, maybe we can provide something they can use from home? But the attendance sheets show they want a physical presence.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
