60,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Wow, look at these! A Maker Workshop, a Digital Archive, Language Circles, or a Mobile Branch. I really love the Mobile Branch idea for the outer wards!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,The Digital Archive Portal sounds like a repeat of the failed digitisation project from six years ago. I find it highly suspect.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,"The Maker Workshop requires tool certification and supervision. Given our retired technician and lack of trained supervisors, it's a logistical nightmare.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,The Mobile Branch is risky. Minako's data on vehicle overruns and Yumi's data on road closures make it financially and operationally unstable.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I still feel the Mobile Branch is the only one that helps the outer wards, but if the roads are closed, it won't work.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Yumi,,What about the Language Learning Circles? They are across the district! That could help the outer wards without needing a big expensive van!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"The Circles align with the ""partner-run"" model that succeeded six years ago. It leverages community organizations rather than internal bureaucracy.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"It also avoids the need for specialized technical certification. If partner organizations provide the facilitators, our staff burden is minimized.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,"From a budget perspective, if these are coordinated with partners, the operational cost is lower than running a vehicle fleet. It's more sustainable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"If the circles are in the neighborhoods, people don't have to take the bus or worry about the roads. I think I like that.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I'm so happy we found something that works for everyone! The Language Circles are friendly, helpful, and reach the people!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It is the only option that avoids the pitfalls of our history and the volatility of our geography. It is the logical choice.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,I concur. It is the most efficient use of our current human resources and avoids the supervision gap.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,It is the most fiscally responsible choice that still meets the community's needs. I am satisfied with this direction.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I feel much better now. It's a kind way to bring people together without leaving anyone out.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I vote for Candidate C, the Language Learning Circles!","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I cast my vote for Candidate C.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shion,,I vote for Candidate C.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,I vote for Candidate C.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I vote for Candidate C.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
